From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mt6878: enable Tetris GNSS transport

Enable the MT6878 GNSS platform device after validating the Nothing OS 4.1
v050 data-link driver probe live on Tetris.

Do not describe external LNA GPIO controls. The pinned B4.1 source disables
its reference LNA block, and the matching stock vendor_boot DTB with each
stock DTBO choice has no GPS pinctrl/LNA wiring records. GPIO143/144 are
not established Tetris wiring; adding named states would permit unchecked
power/wake paths to switch those pins.

The bootloader must still publish the validated GNSS EMI address before a
link may be opened. Transport probe is not navigation or antenna support.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6878-nothing-tetris.dts
@@ -446,6 +446,6 @@
 		emi-alignment = <0x100000>;
 		emi-max-addr = <0xc0000000>;
 		b13b14-status-addr = <0x1c000008>;
-		status = "disabled";
+		status = "okay";
 	};
 };
